{
  "id": "stmt:ema:imfinzi:1:0",
  "type": "Statement",
  "description": "The European Medicines Agency (EMA) has authorized durvalumab in combination with tremelimumab and platinum-based chemotherapy for the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and no sensitizing EGFR mutations or ALK positive mutations. This indication is POSEIDON (NCT03164616), a randomized, multicenter, active-controlled, and open-label study where the specific chemotherapy regime used was based on the histology of the patient's NSCLC.",
